pages.append(page('Daily flow: infants and toddlers',['h','Infants — an individualized responsive cycle'],['p','Arrival and caregiver connection → respond to current feeding/rest/comfort needs → a brief awake interaction or safe floor exploration when available → care and recovery → repeat according to the actual child. Several children can be on different care rhythms. There is no required circle time, academic block or weekly-theme performance.'],['h','Toddlers — a predictable flexible flow'],['table',['Part of the day','Learning opportunity'],[['Arrival','A familiar handoff, comfort and an accessible choice.'],['Play and exploration','Concrete materials, movement, books and short responsive conversations. Repetition is welcome.'],['Outdoor movement','Accessible movement and safe close observation; adjust for weather and individual plans.'],['Care and food','Real participation with adult help; health, hygiene and feeding needs take priority.'],['Rest / quiet','Follow individual needs and actual program requirements; provide appropriate quiet alternatives.'],['Later play and departure','Return to familiar interests, restore together and share a factual family update.']],[125,375]],['p','A transition can carry learning through a word, gesture, useful action or predictable cue. Do not turn every care moment into a quiz or delay care to complete a teaching sequence.']))
pages.append(page('Daily flow: preschool and kindergarten bridge',['p','This is an example organization, not a required clock schedule. Adjust duration, meals, rest, outdoor access and transport to the actual program and children. Keep meaningful play and care central.'],['table',['Example sequence','Purpose / adult role'],[['Arrival and open choices','Welcome families, hear useful information, and support connection.'],['Sustained play / project period','Allow a substantial uninterrupted block when practical; offer brief individual or small-group invitations without rotating every child through the same task.'],['Outdoor movement and inquiry','Support active movement, access, observation and real questions.'],['Meal and care routines','Provide required care, conversation and appropriate participation.'],['Rest / quiet options','Respond to individual needs and actual program/state procedures.'],['Second play / investigation period','Revisit materials, a question, reading/writing purpose or a developing project.'],['Short shared reflection when useful','Children may show, tell, draw, point or choose not to perform.'],['Departure and family connection','Share a specific strength, event or useful support through approved routes.']],[155,345]],['p','For 5- and 6-year-olds, coordinate literacy, mathematics and transition supports with the receiving school. Explicit teaching can help a needed skill; worksheets and timed drills are not the foundation. This bridge has not been checked against a specific state kindergarten standard.']))
