pages.append(page('Families, review and transitions',['h','A useful conversation'],['p','Begin with a specific strength and invite the family’s account. Explain the context and actual support rather than a global label. Ask what the child enjoys, which language or routine is helpful and what priority the family wants heard. An optional home connection should use safe ordinary routines and never require a purchase, project or public disclosure.'],['h','When there is a concern'],['p','Document repeated observations and access/support already tried, separate from interpretation. Talk with the family through the program’s approved process and seek qualified guidance as appropriate. Do not diagnose from a lesson, wait for completion of the curriculum before raising a concern, or present a curriculum status as a screening result.'],['h','A strengths-based transition handoff'],['p','With authorization, share the child’s interests, meaningful work samples, communication strengths, useful supports and the family’s perspective. Include the child’s voice in an accessible form. Keep attendance, health, individual service plans and legally required transfers in their approved systems.'],['h','Privacy'],['p','Use only necessary teaching information. Keep names, photographs, quotations and backups private. The included browser tool stores locally without shared staff accounts, cloud synchronization or application-level encryption. A real multiuser deployment needs separate access, storage, retention and consent decisions.']))
